{"id":"vector-musica","title":"Vector Música","url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Vector_M%C3%BAsica","rev":238901,"fetched":"2026-10-16","lead":[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"b","c":["Vector Música"]}," (formerly known as ",{"t":"b","c":["Música Metro"]},") is a subgenre of ",{"t":"a","c":["Vectordelia"],"id":"vectordelia"}," characterized by a soft, melodic, and feminine visual aesthetic. Unlike the high-contrast and urban style of standard Vectordelia (which utilizes bright CMYK colors and jagged ink splatters) Vector Música employs pastel gradients, smooth curves, and sparkling \"bokeh\" effects to convey whimsy and elegance."]}],"sections":[{"title":"History","id":"history","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["The aesthetic peaked in the late 2000s and early 2010s, finding widespread use in media targeting young girls and teenagers. It was the dominant visual style for the \"Magical Girl\" (Mahō Shōjo) and virtual idol genres of the era, most notably serving as the branding for the music-themed ",{"t":"i","c":["Suite PreCure♪"]}," and the promotional art for the character Musa in ",{"t":"i","c":["Winx Club"]},". The style was also ubiquitous in \"back-to-school\" stationery designs, karaoke interfaces, and background visualizations for rhythm games like ",{"t":"i","c":["Just Dance"]},"."]}]},{"title":"Visuals","id":"visuals","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["The primary compositional element of Vector Música is the curved musical staff (stave), which typically flows across the canvas to guide the viewer's eye. These lines are heavily embellished with scattering music notes, treble clefs, hearts, and floral filigree borrowed from the ",{"t":"a","c":["Vectorbloom"],"id":"vectorbloom"}," aesthetic. While standard Vectordelia often features stark black silhouettes of crowds or breakdancers, Vector Música softens this trope by depicting solitary figures, often wearing headphones or holding microphones, rendered in softer greys or tinted gradients."]}]},{"title":"Media","id":"media","blocks":[{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Anime"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Mermaid Melody Pichi Pichi Pitch"]}," (2003-2005)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Kirarin Revolution"]}," (2006-2007; promo art and openings)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Shugo Chara!"]}," (2007-2008)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Jewelpet"]}," (2009-2010)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Lilpri"]}," (2010-2021)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Suite PreCure♪"]}," (2011-2012)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Pretty Rhythm: Aurora Dream"]}," (2011-2012)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Aikatsu!"]}," (2012-2016)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Love Live! School Idol Project"]}," (2013-2014)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["PriPara"]}," (2014-2017)"]}]},{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Animation"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Class of 3000"]}," (2006-2008)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Tinker Bell"]}," (2008-2009, promotional art and DVD menus)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Winx Club"]}," (2009-2014, seasons 4–5)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Doodlebops Rockin' Road Show"]}," (2010)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Barbie: The Princess & The Popstar"]}," (2012)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["My Little Pony: Rainbow Rocks"]}," (2014)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Lolirock"]}," (2014-present)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["The Music Freaks"]}," (2020-present)"]}]},{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Television"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["The Doodlebops"]}," (2005-2007)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Hannah Montana"]}," (2006-2011, transition graphics)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Victorious"]}," (2010-2013, opening sequence)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["A.N.T. Farm"]}," (2011-2014)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Austin & Ally"]}," (2011-2016)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Violetta"]}," (2012-2015)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Soy Luna"]}," (2016-2026)"]}]},{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Video Games"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Hatsune Miku: Project DIVA"]}," (2009)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Just Dance"]}," (2009-present)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Hatsune Miku: Project DIVA 2nd"]}," (2010)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Love Live! School Idol Festival"]}," (2